## Narrative
The bucket policy classifier treats any aws:SourceIp IpAddress clause as non-public if the value parses as a fixed CIDR. The helper only checks that the prefix parses as u8, so a full-range CIDR like 0.0.0.0/0 passes and is treated as restricting. The BlockPublicPolicy guardrail depends on parsed_policy.is_public(), so this misclassification can allow a public policy to be accepted even when BlockPublicPolicy is enabled. The path is reachable only to the bucket owner principal and affects public access controls, not cross-tenant authorization.
