# Resolution
Fixed in commit `ca5911f` (`auth: match S3 SourceIp public policy rules`).

The resolution replaced the old `aws:SourceIp` classifier, which accepted any
syntactically valid CIDR as non-public, with AWS-aligned threshold logic:
IPv4 CIDRs are only non-public when they are `/8` or narrower or entirely
within RFC1918 private space, and IPv6 CIDRs are only non-public when they
are `/32` or narrower. That closes the BlockPublicPolicy bypass for broad
ranges such as `0.0.0.0/0` and `::/0`, and also fixes the persisted
`bucket_policy_public` bit used by `GetBucketPolicyStatus` and
`RestrictPublicBuckets`.

Regression coverage was added in local unit tests and in AWS-backed
`s3-tests`. The AWS compatibility runs confirmed the intended behavior for
`0.0.0.0/0`, `11.0.0.0/7`, `11.0.0.0/8`, and `fd00::/8`.
